### Day 4/50 — Databases

Data, by itself, can be messy.
Thousands of names,
Numbers,
Dates,
Details.

All existing — 
but without any order,
finding meaning in them would be chaos.

That's why we create **databases**.
Not to create more information,
but to give the information a place.

Maybe that's the **beauty of organization.**

The things themselves don't change.

A book is still a book.
A file is still a file.
A piece of data is still the same.

But put everything in the right place 
and suddenly,
chaos becomes something you can understand.

** Sometimes, we don't need more.
We just need to put what we already have in the right place.**
